Z||000004||sqoach||09-21-2001||12:47 PM||||Must be the turn signal switch itself. I've never changed one, so I don't know what to tell you. But that's what I would check next.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||thomas_l||09-21-2001||01:07 PM||||Probably a bad flasher. When you turn on the 4 way you are closing both contacts in the t/s switch but using a different flasher due to the higher current draw. I think I saw them mounted ahead of the passenger door in the way of my heater core job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
